  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.2.0: Added built-in observability. TaskQueue and TaskRunWithTimeout emit OpenTelemetry-shaped metrics and traces through the BCL Meter and ActivitySource named TaskHandler (queue depth, concurrency in use, per-stage durations, outcomes, rejections, cancellations, errors by type), with trace context propagated from enqueue into task code. New TaskQueue.Name and TaskQueueOptions.Name label each queue. No new runtime dependency on net8.0+; netstandard targets add System.Diagnostics.DiagnosticSource. See TELEMETRY.md. v2.1.1: Fixed result-returning EnqueueAsync<T> overloads so that a task exceeding its timeout completes the TaskHandle<T> with a TimeoutException (previously it double-completed the handle, surfacing a cancellation plus an InvalidOperationException fault). Hardened TaskHandle<T> completion to be idempotent. Updated System.Threading.Channels and Microsoft.Bcl.AsyncInterfaces to 10.0.11. v2.1.0: Retargeted to net8.0 and net10.0 (dropped net6.0); still supports netstandard2.0 and netstandard2.1. v2.0.0: Event-driven architecture (10-100x faster), async API (StartAsync, StopAsync, DisposeAsync), task results (TaskHandle<T>), priorities, timeouts, statistics, progress reporting. BREAKING: Removed IterationDelayMs and QueuedTasks properties.",
